fcalc> h(2)
20
fcalc> ! A function may call others, defined before or after it.
fcalc> twice(n) = 2 * later(n)
twice(n) = 2 * later(n)
fcalc> later(n) = n + 1
later(n) = n + 1
fcalc> twice(5)
12
fcalc> ! Recursion: IF evaluates only the arm it chooses, so a function can stop.
fcalc> fact(n) = if(n < 2, 1, n * fact(n - 1))
fact(n) = if(n < 2, 1, n * fact(n - 1))
fcalc> fact(5)
